# Project context

This repo is **personal** Lua code for [CC: Tweaked](https://tweaked.cc/) (ComputerCraft Tweaked) used **inside** the [TerraFirmaGreg Modern](https://github.com/TerraFirmaGreg-Team/Modpack-Modern/) modpack — not contribution to the modpack itself.

## Environment

- Minecraft **1.20.1**, Forge/NeoForge pack: TerraFirmaCraft + GregTech Modern (+ Create/Greate, AE2, Ad Astra, etc.)
- Runtime: computers / turtles / pocket computers from **CC: Tweaked**
- Pack may include GregTech peripherals and UTF-8 support for ComputerCraft — prefer APIs and peripherals available in TFG, not vanilla-only assumptions

## How to write code

- Target **CC: Tweaked Lua** (Lua 5.2-style subset used by CC), not general Lua/LuaJIT desktop apps
- Prefer clear, practical scripts for factory automation, monitoring, logistics, and GT/TFC integration in-world
- Keep scripts self-contained or with simple `require` modules suitable for copying onto computers in-game
- Do not treat this as pack KubeJS/config work unless the user asks
- Keep craft/transfer helpers inventory-agnostic: callers pass peripheral names (`from` / `out` / `machine`), never hard-code specific storage blocks
- Greenhouse control lives in `greenhouse.lua`; `grow` recipes in `recipes.cfg` are started from recursive `craft.request`
- Two configs: `recipes.cfg` (machines/IO/flags) and `storage.cfg` (main/flora/overflow/sources/seeds/routes/UI timings)
- `greenhouse_clean.lua` is autonomous — any computer with configs + peripheral network; not tied to `craft_ui`
- Non-fridge items (e.g. `firmalife:spice/basil_leaves`) use `route` → `overflow` in `storage.cfg`; cleaner drains overflow first
